/*
  AISoftwareUpdateChangelogSummarizer.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0048 · AISoftwareUpdateChangelogSummarizer (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `AISoftwareUpdateChangelogSummarizer` resolves (table "AISoftwareUpdateChangelogSummarizer") lives
  here with its web English value. These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master
  catalog at integration time; they are kept in a per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt
  owns its own strings without editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the parity set extracted from the web source
  (web/src/components/ai/AISoftwareUpdateChangelogSummarizer.tsx + the shared AIFeatureCard /
  AiOutputPanel / AIThinkingIndicator literals it composes). The second group backs the native P4
  leaf chrome (the freshness / connectivity / loading / error copy) so the Swift sources hold no
  English prose.
*/

/* --- Parity: the web source's t(key, default) calls --- */
"softwareUpdates.aiNarration.title" = "Summarize my software update history";
"softwareUpdates.aiNarration.description" = "Ask Helix to walk through your firmware update history — the current version, the install cadence, and the headline release-note themes. The narrator quotes only the deterministic update events your vehicle reported plus public Tesla release notes for the versions you have installed; it never invents firmware versions or claims features your installed build does not have.";
"softwareUpdates.aiNarration.button" = "Summarize updates";
"softwareUpdates.aiNarration.badge" = "Helix";
"softwareUpdates.aiNarration.noVehicleHint" = "Pick a vehicle above to enable Helix.";

